/target

# The compiler is never in git. It is built into target/ from the pinned recipe
# by `cargo xtask fetch-toolchain`, and published as a release artefact by CI.
# These are here as a second line of defence: `cargo xtask check-hygiene` fails
# the build if anything toolchain-shaped is tracked, wherever it lives.
**/toolchain/bin/
**/toolchain/inc/
**/toolchain/lib/
**/toolchain/doc/
**/toolchain/fbc
**/toolchain/fbc.exe
*.7z
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.a
*.o
*.ttf
*.otf

# Generated for one specific fetched bundle; a release regenerates it.
/crates/etb-gui/assets/toolchain-manifest.txt

**/*.rs.bk

# Programs other people wrote are tested from where they live, never from here
# (see crates/etb-testkit/tests/local_corpus.rs).
/local-corpus/

# The Windows test VM: disk images, firmware vars, ISOs and its own SSH key.
# Scaffolding only — nothing in here is part of a release.
/vm/
